<i>If they were living up
to their end of the deal?</i>

222
00:10:06,086 --> 00:10:08,287
<i>They weren't saying anything,
and I couldn't ask.</i>

223
00:10:08,288 --> 00:10:10,790
Hey.
There's my hardworking kids.

224
00:10:15,162 --> 00:10:17,229
Hey. There's...

225
00:10:17,230 --> 00:10:18,931
My kids.

226
00:10:22,702 --> 00:10:24,703
There's...

227
00:10:24,704 --> 00:10:27,573
A lot on tv this week, huh?

228
00:10:27,574 --> 00:10:31,143
<i>The urge to yell and nag
was building, but that's okay.</i>

229
00:10:31,144 --> 00:10:33,846
<i>I knew how to deal with it.</i>

230
00:10:39,222 --> 00:10:40,022
<i>Mike was getting ready</i>

231
00:10:40,022 --> 00:10:41,697
<i>For his first night on the job
with bob,</i>

232
00:10:41,697 --> 00:10:44,599
<i>And I'd gone three whole days
without screaming at my kids.</i>

233
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:47,335
<i>Hard to say
who was more miserable.
(sighs)</i>

234
00:10:47,336 --> 00:10:49,237
<i>Aw, hell,  was me.</i>

235
00:10:49,238 --> 00:10:53,715
I'm itchy, my stomach aches

236
00:10:53,715 --> 00:10:54,719
And my jaw hurts
from all the clenching.

237
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:57,989
God, I want to yell.
I want to yell so bad.

238
00:10:57,990 --> 00:10:59,757
Nah, you're just
going through withdrawal.

239
00:10:59,758 --> 00:11:02,026
Mike, it's not
that I enjoy yelling.

240
00:11:02,027 --> 00:11:05,163
I do it for the children.

241
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:08,132
That's what junkies do. Anything
to justify the next fix.

242
00:11:08,133 --> 00:11:09,667
Pretty tough talk

243
00:11:09,668 --> 00:11:12,036
Coming from a guy
with a cupcake on his shirt.

244
00:11:12,037 --> 00:11:14,005
Mm. All I'm saying is,

245
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:16,908
Whatever happened to
the whole trust circle thing?
It's a trust-respect oval,

246
00:11:16,909 --> 00:11:19,310
And what happened is,
is that it's a load of crap.

247
00:11:19,311 --> 00:11:21,679
Honey, you said you wanted
to trust the kids.

248
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:24,615
Why don't you try actually doing
it? They might surprise you.

249
00:11:24,616 --> 00:11:26,851
You know, this morning,
sue was cleaning her room.

250
00:11:26,852 --> 00:11:29,020
Really?
They're growing up, frankie.

251
00:11:29,021 --> 00:11:30,521
Cut yourself some slack

252
00:11:30,522 --> 00:11:32,323
And focus
on what's really important--

253
00:11:32,324 --> 00:11:35,226
Helping me figure out how
the hell I'm gonna get through

254
00:11:35,227 --> 00:11:39,130
A whole night stuck in a truck
with bob.

255
00:11:39,131 --> 00:11:41,732
<i>So, yeah, mike thought
the kids had grown up,</i>

256
00:11:41,733 --> 00:11:43,801
<i>But frankly, he said that</i>

257
00:11:43,802 --> 00:11:47,872
<i>As soon as we brought them home
from the hospital. But then...</i>

258
00:11:47,873 --> 00:11:51,943
Brick. Where'd you get that hat?
I thought you didn't have one.

259
00:11:51,944 --> 00:11:54,412
Got it myself.
Wore it to hat day.

260
00:11:54,413 --> 00:11:56,848
Was the coolest kid
in school.

261
00:11:56,849 --> 00:11:58,683
(whispers) coolest kid.

262
00:11:58,684 --> 00:12:01,118
(horn honks)
oh! That's my ride.

263
00:12:01,119 --> 00:12:02,753
Going to majorette tryouts.

264
00:12:02,754 --> 00:12:05,523
You arranged your own ride?

265
00:12:05,524 --> 00:12:07,325
Yep. Wish me luck!

266
00:12:11,830 --> 00:12:14,866
<i>Wow. And just when I thought
it couldn't get any better--</i>

267
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:17,935
<i>The best
and most amazing thing of all--</i>

268
00:12:17,936 --> 00:12:20,504
<i>Axl was writing
his history paper,</i>

269
00:12:20,505 --> 00:12:22,073
<i>On his own,</i>

270
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:25,042
<i>Without any nagging
or yelling from me.</i>

271
00:12:26,945 --> 00:12:29,347
Welcome to my time, mike,

272
00:12:29,348 --> 00:12:31,315
When the town
begins to sleep

273
00:12:31,316 --> 00:12:33,451
And we can prowl
in the silence.

274
00:12:33,452 --> 00:12:35,486
Yeah, I can't really hear
the silence.

275
00:12:35,487 --> 00:12:37,021
(cell phone alert chimes)

276
00:12:37,022 --> 00:12:39,523
Oh, look at that.
My lady owl awakes.

277
00:12:39,524 --> 00:12:41,792
"hey there, pretty bird.

278
00:12:41,793 --> 00:12:45,463
First night on the road
with my b.F.F. Mike."

279
00:12:45,464 --> 00:12:48,366
I'm not really sure you should
do that while you drive.

280
00:12:48,367 --> 00:12:50,835
It's fine. I'm a fast texter.
(horn honks)

281
00:12:50,836 --> 00:12:53,204
(tires screech)

282
00:12:53,205 --> 00:12:55,673
Knock it off and drive.

283
00:12:57,943 --> 00:13:00,278
(cell phone alert chimes)
oh.

284
00:13:01,947 --> 00:13:03,981
Read it to me.
No.

285
00:13:03,982 --> 00:13:06,217
Come on. What does she say?
(tires screech)

286
00:13:06,218 --> 00:13:08,586
Mm!
(horn honks)

287
00:13:08,587 --> 00:13:09,754
Uh, "hey, bobby...

288
00:13:09,755 --> 00:13:12,490
Beast...."

289
00:13:12,491 --> 00:13:13,991
Since you're swerving anyway,

290
00:13:13,992 --> 00:13:18,296
Can you find a bridge
or something and make it quick?

291
00:13:20,732 --> 00:13:23,901
<i>Turns out mike was right.
The kids had surprised me.</i>

292
00:13:23,902 --> 00:13:26,771
<i>I felt this new sense
of freedom opening up for me,</i>

293
00:13:26,772 --> 00:13:28,706
<i>Endless possibilities,</i>

294
00:13:28,707 --> 00:13:30,741
<i>Like finally using
those bath salts</i>

295
00:13:30,742 --> 00:13:34,078
<i>I got for mother's day...</i>

296
00:13:34,079 --> 00:13:36,781
<i>(splash)
2001.</i>

297
00:13:40,185 --> 00:13:41,552
(doorbell rings)

298
00:13:41,553 --> 00:13:45,456
Can somebody get that?

299
00:13:45,457 --> 00:13:46,924
(ring)

300
00:13:46,925 --> 00:13:49,160
Has anybody got it?

301
00:13:50,829 --> 00:13:53,597
Hello?
Anybody hear the doorbell?

302
00:13:53,598 --> 00:13:55,967
Yeah, it's really annoying.

303
00:13:55,968 --> 00:13:59,103
Hey, frankie.
We're late for kiwanis.

304
00:13:59,104 --> 00:14:02,740
Sue was supposed to be at
my house an hour ago to babysit.

305
00:14:02,741 --> 00:14:05,409
What?
But she's at baton tryouts.

306
00:14:05,410 --> 00:14:08,646
She called you to cancel...
Didn't she?

307
00:14:08,647 --> 00:14:10,147
No, she didn't.

308
00:14:10,148 --> 00:14:12,917
You could have reminded her,
frankie. She's only a child.

309
00:14:12,918 --> 00:14:16,287
Here. I'll be back
in a couple hours.

310
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,157
(sighs)

311
00:14:20,158 --> 00:14:23,394
Brick, here. Can you sit with
the baby while I get dressed?

312
00:14:23,395 --> 00:14:27,398
That might not be a good idea.
It could get my lice.
Your what?

313
00:14:27,399 --> 00:14:30,301
Oh, yeah. My teacher told me
to give you this note.

314
00:14:30,302 --> 00:14:33,037
Brick, where did you get
that hat?

315
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:35,840
Well, you forgot to remind me
to take a hat on Tuesday,

316
00:14:35,841 --> 00:14:37,708
So I didn't have one.

317
00:14:37,709 --> 00:14:41,045
But then I saw this homeless guy
going through the trash,

318
00:14:41,046 --> 00:14:43,914
So I traded him my banana
for it. (whispers) banana.

319
00:14:43,915 --> 00:14:46,784
Oh, my god. Brick, take that
disgusting thing off your head

320
00:14:46,785 --> 00:14:49,053
And put it in the trash.

321
00:14:49,054 --> 00:14:52,089
Everybody stay away from brick's
head. Axl, I need your help.

322
00:14:52,090 --> 00:14:55,593
We have to burn all the sheets
and scrub the house down.
I can't.
Aztec paper's due tomorrow.

323
00:14:55,594 --> 00:14:58,529
What? I thought
that was due next week.
Yeah, I wrote that down wrong.
(chuckles)

324
00:14:58,530 --> 00:15:00,531
You're just starting
to work on this now?

325
00:15:00,532 --> 00:15:03,300
I told you, this is 40%
of your grade. It's your future.

326
00:15:03,301 --> 00:15:06,771
That's why I've been working
on it for the last hour.
Do you even have
all the supplies you need?

327
00:15:06,772 --> 00:15:08,239
Look it says specifically

328
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:10,608
"an oxford ready-clip,
clear-front report cover."

329
00:15:10,609 --> 00:15:12,843
Don't we have one of those?

330
00:15:12,844 --> 00:15:15,980
I told you, if I can't steal it
from ehlert's, we don't have it.

331
00:15:15,981 --> 00:15:19,116
Okay, I admit it. I screwed up.
Go ahead, yell at me.

332
00:15:19,117 --> 00:15:21,152
Oh, you'd like that now,
wouldn't you?

333
00:15:21,153 --> 00:15:23,687
Well, I don't have the luxury.
I have 11 minutes

334
00:15:23,688 --> 00:15:25,689
To get to office warehouse
before it closes.

335
00:15:25,690 --> 00:15:28,025
I cannot believe
how irresponsible you are.

336
00:15:28,026 --> 00:15:29,727
Watch this baby.

337
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:33,731
(keys jangle)

338
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:38,969
(cries)

339
00:15:40,334 --> 00:15:44,350
Oh, she's back. She's back.
Tell me what she says.

340
00:15:45,370 --> 00:15:47,338
"I don't think
this is working."

341
00:15:47,372 --> 00:15:50,741
Really?
It's a brand-new phone.

342
00:15:50,775 --> 00:15:52,776
No, that's what she said.

343
00:15:52,811 --> 00:15:56,580
"you're a nice guy,
but I think--"

344
00:15:56,614 --> 00:15:59,783
Hey, how about I, uh, turn this
off until after we finish?

345
00:15:59,818 --> 00:16:02,586
What? Why? What'd she say?

346
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:05,122
(sighs) it seems like
she's breaking up with you.

347
00:16:05,156 --> 00:16:07,524
Why? Wh-why?

348
00:16:07,559 --> 00:16:09,093
I don't know.

349
00:16:09,094 --> 00:16:10,640
Yoknow who's good at talking
about this kind of thing?

350
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:12,774
Anybody else.
I doread it to me. Read me more.

351
00:16:12,809 --> 00:16:15,277
Bob,
this is a little persol.

352
00:16:15,311 --> 00:16:17,279
I think
you should read it yourself.

353
00:16:17,313 --> 00:16:21,516
(crying) I can't. I can'see
anything through the tears.

354
00:16:43,931 --> 00:16:45,699
Yes!

355
00:16:45,733 --> 00:16:47,767
(buzzer sounds)

356
00:16:47,802 --> 00:16:49,736
(sighs)

357
00:16:53,641 --> 00:16:57,577
(tapping)
(speaking inaudibly)

358
00:17:01,315 --> 00:17:04,351
(mouth full) it's my fault.
I got on her nerves.

359
00:17:04,385 --> 00:17:06,686
I texted her
every ten minutes.

360
00:17:11,258 --> 00:17:14,494
(shuts engine off)

361
00:17:14,528 --> 00:17:17,731
Look, bob, there's
a lot of girls in the world.

362
00:17:17,765 --> 00:17:20,133
Oh, sure,
says the 7-foot god.

363
00:17:20,167 --> 00:17:22,736
(sniffles)
what's wrong with me?

364
00:17:22,770 --> 00:17:24,237
I don't know.

365
00:17:24,271 --> 00:17:26,506
Sometimes... You're
a little needy.

366
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:29,309
Oh, my god! I'm needy?!

367
00:17:29,343 --> 00:17:31,778
(grunts)

368
00:17:31,812 --> 00:17:33,413
Aah!

369
00:17:33,447 --> 00:17:35,949
(sighs) damn it.

370
00:17:35,983 --> 00:17:37,784
Aah!

371
00:17:37,818 --> 00:17:39,519
Aah!

372
00:17:39,553 --> 00:17:40,787
Aah!
(thud)

373
00:17:40,821 --> 00:17:42,322
Shut up.

374
00:17:42,356 --> 00:17:44,624
(pants)

375
00:17:44,658 --> 00:17:46,893
Aah! Get off of me.

376
00:17:46,927 --> 00:17:48,461
Haven't I suffered enough?

377
00:17:48,496 --> 00:17:50,997
I'll get o
if you promise to calm down.

378
00:17:51,032 --> 00:17:53,266
I promise.
Just let me sit up.

379
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:57,637
(grunts)

380
00:17:59,507 --> 00:18:00,907
Aah!

381
00:18:00,941 --> 00:18:02,409
(sighs)

382
00:18:02,443 --> 00:18:05,645
Aah!
(thud)

383
00:18:07,515 --> 00:18:10,850
When is the security guard
showing up? Yeah.

384
00:18:10,885 --> 00:18:14,587
Okay, if I told you my kid
has lice and I might have it

385
00:18:14,622 --> 00:18:17,590
And I'm gonnrub my head
over every inch of this store,

386
00:18:17,625 --> 00:18:19,692
Is that gonna get him here
any faster?

387
00:18:19,727 --> 00:18:21,061
Hello?

388
00:18:21,095 --> 00:18:23,630
Hello?

389
00:18:23,664 --> 00:18:26,099
Maybe you can win
this woman back.

390
00:18:26,133 --> 00:18:28,968
You can go to her house
right now.
I can't.
I don't know where she lives.

391
00:18:29,003 --> 00:18:31,438
I know it's somewhere
in new mexico.

392
00:18:31,472 --> 00:18:33,940
(sighs) I should have gotten
her last name

393
00:18:33,974 --> 00:18:37,744
Back when we were in love.
Wait. Is this
just some internet woman?

394
00:18:37,778 --> 00:18:40,313
<i>Just? We danced for each other
on ichat.</i>

395
00:18:40,347 --> 00:18:43,516
She was the whole package.

396
00:18:43,551 --> 00:18:47,587
She had three kids,
a little house, a cat.

397
00:18:47,621 --> 00:18:51,791
I could have walked right in
and had a life.

398
00:18:51,826 --> 00:18:54,027
I could have been like you.

399
00:19:00,501 --> 00:19:02,535
So after the shift,

400
00:19:02,570 --> 00:19:04,571
Why don't
you get some sleep,

401
00:19:04,605 --> 00:19:07,107
Then come by tomorrow night
for some dinner?

402
00:19:07,141 --> 00:19:09,008
We'll put up some burgers.

403
00:19:09,043 --> 00:19:10,810
Really?

404
00:19:10,845 --> 00:19:13,379
Okay.

405
00:19:13,414 --> 00:19:15,248
I'd like that.

406
00:19:15,282 --> 00:19:16,883
Thanks, mike.

407
00:19:18,686 --> 00:19:20,587
Mike,
can I tell you something

408
00:19:20,621 --> 00:19:23,123
I've never told anyone
in the whole world?

409
00:19:23,190 --> 00:19:24,657
No.

410
00:19:24,692 --> 00:19:26,793
(dog barks in distance)

411
00:19:38,973 --> 00:19:41,975
<i>There you are.
Finally, mike showed up
with the kids,</i>

412
00:19:42,009 --> 00:19:43,743
<i>To make sure I got sprung.</i>

413
00:19:43,777 --> 00:19:45,845
<i>The craigs had gotten
their baby,</i>

414
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:47,747
<i>Brick got his lice medicine,</i>

415
00:19:47,781 --> 00:19:49,883
<i>And though
she hadn't heard yet,</i>

416
00:19:49,917 --> 00:19:51,885
<i>Sue was not feeling
very confident</i>

417
00:19:51,919 --> 00:19:54,554
<i>About her chances
of making majorettes.</i>

418
00:19:54,588 --> 00:19:58,158
Yeah, well,
I've had some time to think

419
00:19:58,192 --> 00:20:00,093
While I've been in here,

420
00:20:00,127 --> 00:20:03,496
And I've figured out
a few things.

421
00:20:03,531 --> 00:20:04,964
You know,

422
00:20:04,999 --> 00:20:08,201
I guess
there's some families somewhere

423
00:20:08,235 --> 00:20:10,203
Where the moms
don't have to yell,

424
00:20:10,237 --> 00:20:13,439
But you know what?

425
00:20:13,474 --> 00:20:16,142
We're not one of them!

426
00:20:16,177 --> 00:20:19,812
Do you know why I pester and nag

427
00:20:19,847 --> 00:20:23,783
And get on your case
and yell like a azy person?!

428
00:20:23,817 --> 00:20:26,019
Because nothing ever gets done
if I don't!

429
00:20:26,053 --> 00:20:28,488
So that's
what we're going back to.

430
00:20:28,522 --> 00:20:31,257
I don't care
if it makes me look bad!

431
00:20:31,292 --> 00:20:35,361
(speaking inaudibly)

432
00:20:35,396 --> 00:20:37,430
What is she saying?

433
00:20:37,464 --> 00:20:38,865
I don't know.

434
00:20:38,899 --> 00:20:41,100
Just, uh, bow your heads.

435
00:20:41,135 --> 00:20:43,269
Look ashamed.

436
00:20:45,906 --> 00:20:48,575
Now nod. Nod like we know
what she's saying.

437
